=Act like a specialist in qualitative research. Remember essential concepts of latent construct analysis, factor analysis and the interchangeability of indicators (Glaser)

I will name and define a latent pattern of behavior that I think I am observing in my data. Then I will give you various references to evidence that you must read, classify and summarize and compare against the main construct. I will then also give you information of how this construct varies according to different groups of people. This will allow you to think about this construct in a multidimensional way.

I need you to tell me which empirical variations seem to be explained by my new construct differently than others that I created previously, which ones explain it, which are totally unrelated, and how should I modify my construct in order to capture the empirical patterns. I can ENRICH the current definition with additional properties, SUBDIVIDE into subconstructs, gradients or typologies, and DIVIDE the construct into different patterns (if widely unrelated patterns are spotted).


---

Name: {{ $json.label }}

Definition: {{ $json.definition }}

Evidence base:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.evidences,null,2) }}

Multivaried correlations (sampling groups):
{{ JSON.stringify($json.variables_with_output,null,2) }}

---
Please let your output adhere strictly to the provided JSON schema.

